<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-631260ddd57a47799fe2f421c14f8fec" title="sat-c2-u07-salient.html qc1" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>B</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;salient&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The chef&apos;s salient ingredient is unlisted on the menu and undetectable in the finished dish.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">Of the witness&apos;s forty minutes on the stand, the salient moment came when she admitted she never saw the driver.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">The committee spent an hour on salient trivia — font sizes and paper-clip counts that decided nothing at all.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">Reviewers called the new sedan thoroughly salient: identical to its rivals, with nothing about it worth remarking on.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Salient means standing out as most noticeable and most important, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because an ingredient kept unlisted and undetectable is hidden by design — a salient one would be impossible to miss.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Salient means standing out as most noticeable and most important, so it&apos;s the correct answer because that one admission leaps out of forty minutes of testimony and changes what the whole case is worth.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Salient means standing out as most noticeable and most important, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because the sentence itself says these details decided nothing — trivia that carries no weight fails salient&apos;s importance test.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Salient means standing out as most noticeable and most important, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a car identical to its rivals, with nothing worth remarking on, has no feature that stands out at all.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
